## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to design a compact prefix-search data structure and implement tie-breaking logic using a Trie.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with terminal frequencies stored at each node
- Prefix search via traversal to the prefix end node
- DFS collection of all words in the subtree
- Sorting by frequency (descending), then lexicographic order for ties

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.freq = 0;
  }
}

class Autocomplete {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  addWord(word, freq) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    node.freq = freq;
  }

  getSuggestions(prefix, limit) {
    if (limit <= 0) return [];

    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) return [];
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }

    const results = [];
    const dfs = (currentNode, path) => {
      if (currentNode.freq > 0) {
        results.push({ word: path, freq: currentNode.freq });
      }
      for (const [char, childNode] of currentNode.children) {
        dfs(childNode, path + char);
      }
    };

    dfs(node, prefix);

    results.sort((a, b) => {
      if (b.freq !== a.freq) return b.freq - a.freq;
      return a.word.localeCompare(b.word);
    });

    return results.slice(0, limit).map(r => r.word);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply DFS for topological ordering and then DP-style relaxation on a DAG to compute shortest paths without a heap. Also checks path reconstruction via a parent array.

## Key Concepts

- DFS-based topological sort
- DAG single-source shortest path via relaxation in topo order
- Path reconstruction with a parent array
- Complexity: O(n+m)

## Code Example

```javascript
function shortestPathDAG(n, edges, start, target) {
  const g = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) g[u].push([v, w]);
  const visited = Array(n).fill(false);
  const topo = [];
  function dfs(u){
    visited[u] = true;
    for (const [v] of g[u]) if (!visited[v]) dfs(v);
    topo.push(u);
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (!visited[i]) dfs(i);
  topo.reverse();
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = Array(n).fill(INF);
  const parent = Array(n).fill(-1);
  dist[start] = 0;
  for (const u of topo) {
    if (dist[u] === INF) continue;
    for (const [v, w] of g[u]) {
      if (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + w;
        parent[v] = u;
      }
    }
  }
  if (dist[target] === INF) return {time: -1, path: []};
  const path = [];
  for (let x = target; x != -1; x = parent[x]) path.push(x);
  path.reverse();
  return {time: dist[target], path};
}
```

